  "details": "This is something I've always thought about and it's very ambitious. Two avatar systems and It goes like this: \nEvery user must have a standardized human avatar made from an adopted avatar system by VRChat. This first system provides different colors, hair styles, clothing ...etc. The user can also choose to use this avatar or any other user-made avatars in VRChat which is the already available system now. \nHowever, any user has the option to only see the standardized avatars of others if they want to. This will solve so many issues that have to do with Quest compatibility, big avatar sizes, shader and crashing problems. Also, a world or game creator or even an event host can choose that only standardized avatars are used in their creations to avoid cheating or ruining the experience for others.",
